        "passages": [
          "For an eligible runtime-capable machine, evaluation produces exactly the value\nthat target execution would produce with the same arguments, selected\nconformances/providers, and target semantics. Evaluation changes when, not what.\nProof-only machines need no runtime representation but obey the same core value\nsemantics and cannot observe the compiler phase."
        ],
        "reason": "The original const-name place reaches an admitted selected generic implementation but the checked-tree interpreter executes its map row template instead of the call's prepared capture entry, leaving Value unbound. Semantic evaluation must execute the same selected concrete invocation as runtime without changing admission or public guarantee identity.",
        "revision": "bfcffe6bcfcedb6fd60713e223408566c6c4e10d"
